<item>
            <title>[LU-20360] tunefs.lustre silently ignores --mountfsoptions-only changes</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20360</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;tunefs.lustre exits with rc 0 without writing anything when --mountfsoptions&lt;br/&gt;
is the only change, silently discarding the new mount options (old options&lt;br/&gt;
still used on next mount).&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reproduce:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;tunefs.lustre --mountfsoptions=&amp;lt;new opts&amp;gt; /dev/XXX &#160;(no other option)&lt;br/&gt;
then --print shows the opts unchanged. Adding any other option (e.g. --param)&lt;br/&gt;
makes it persist.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Found by commit-hunter-v1.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
